  "result": "The rule and its witnesses for `LVMC_11_38_030` pass the gate: it returned **OK** on the first run (5 witnesses, 6 names, composes nothing). That used 1 of the 6 runs.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_38_030.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** x is in the motorcycle aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle`), or is a moped, or is an electric scooter.\n- **When it applies:** the observation is inside city limits (`asm.within_city_limits`).\n- **The duty:** x must not be both moving faster than `p.speed_resolution` and overlapping any sidewalk region.\n- **Choices:** the node left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings. The \"be ridden means moving\" reading is already on the node's record, so I didn't repeat it.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_38_030.lean`) use a roadway with one lane and a sidewalk alongside. Every scene is inside city limits.\n\n| Scenario | Scene | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | motorcycle on the sidewalk at 2 m/s | violated |\n| permit | motorcycle in the lane at 10 m/s | compliant |\n| idle | bicycle on the sidewalk | not applicable |\n| blind | moped moving at the curb, sidewalk occupancy masked | unknown |\n| branch_1 | motorcycle parked on the sidewalk at 0 m/s | compliant |\n\nBefore the gate run I sent one shell command that also listed the Core folder. The permission layer blocked it, so nothing ran, and I used the Read tool instead. `task_result.md` mentions this.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
